1
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:15,501
Friends, I cannot ignore this growing
conflict, or rather what I would call

2
00:00:15,501 --> 00:00:17,080
the growing harassment

3
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:24,600
of Academician Robert Iskanderovich
Nigmatulin. We have repeatedly seen

4
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:31,800
his very bold, critical statements
about the situation in our country

5
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:38,558
and the actions of the authorities.
Robert Iskanderovich spoke openly about

6
00:00:38,558 --> 00:00:40,720
it at this year's Moscow

7
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:48,240
Economic Forum. Over several
years I have interviewed

8
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:58,280
Robert Iskanderovich several times. I deeply
respect him and consider him a scrupulously

9
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:08,440
honest scientist of the Soviet school, a Soviet
man. And what I see now—the harassment unfolding

10
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:14,251
before my eyes against Robert
Nigmatulin—cannot leave me indifferent.

11
00:01:14,251 --> 00:01:16,440
We know about the conflict

12
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:22,200
between one, or perhaps both,
of the Kovalchuk brothers.

13
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:29,400
I mean Mikhail Kovalchuk, who heads the Kurchatov
Center, and the Russian academic community,

14
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:35,370
the Russian Academy of Sciences and a
number of scientific institutes that

15
00:01:35,370 --> 00:01:38,920
are to be placed under
the Kurchatov Center.

16
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:47,720
One explanation is that this was intended
to allow Kovalchuk, one of the brothers,

17
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:52,282
to concentrate a substantial scientific
resource in his hands, reorganize the

18
00:01:52,282 --> 00:01:54,000
management of Russian science

19
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,640
and place that management in Mikhail Kovalchuk's
hands. As we know, the Kovalchuk brothers

20
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:05,960
have very close relations with the country's
leadership, particularly President Putin.

21
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:12,600
Their acquaintance goes back many years, to the
1990s; one can recall the Ozero cooperative.

22
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:23,640
And the Kovalchuks, as I understand
from various insider circles,

23
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:31,509
have considerable influence over
Vladimir Putin. Putin listens to their

24
00:02:31,509 --> 00:02:34,280
views, and so the process

25
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:38,762
of reorganizing Russian science
proposed by Mikhail Kovalchuk was

26
00:02:38,762 --> 00:02:40,520
received favorably by Putin.

27
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:48,320
He gave Mishustin the corresponding instruction,
and the process began. But the process met

28
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:53,960
resistance from Russia's scientific community.
This concerns more than Nigmatulin:

29
00:02:53,960 --> 00:03:01,360
several well-known Russian scientists, professors
and members of the Russian Academy of Sciences

30
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:09,080
spoke out against the change. I don't want to
go into the substance of the conflict now.

31
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:16,080
You can look it up online and learn for
yourselves how the conflict developed.

32
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:25,880
What I do want to say is that I am
deeply outraged. As I understand it,

33
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:33,200
the Kovalchuks encountered repeated
resistance from Robert Nigmatulin.

34
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:41,680
Nigmatulin publicly addressed Kovalchuk
and publicly expressed his position.

35
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:46,307
Now, I believe, the administrative
machinery is being deployed against

36
00:03:46,307 --> 00:03:47,960
Nigmatulin in full force.

37
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:55,760
And in the rag—I can call it
nothing else—Moskovsky Komsomolets,

38
00:03:55,760 --> 00:04:02,460
which, along with Komsomolskaya
Pravda, is a mouthpiece

39
00:04:02,460 --> 00:04:08,200
of domestic propaganda; they are links in
the same chain of pro-government media,

40
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:13,281
a smear article has appeared under
the title “The Octopus in the Russian

41
00:04:13,281 --> 00:04:16,880
Academy of Sciences,” in
which Robert Iskanderovich

42
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:23,480
is quite literally smeared. Let
me read you a short excerpt:

43
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:27,237
“The Russian Academy of Sciences has
been shaken by corruption scandals. In

44
00:04:27,237 --> 00:04:29,240
the spring, two employees of the Academy

45
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:32,762
were arrested for accepting bribes.
Recently a court extended the house

46
00:04:32,762 --> 00:04:34,200
arrest of a senior researcher

47
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:38,280
at the Institute of Philosophy, Svetlana
Mesyats, accused of large-scale fraud

48
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:44,038
involving a government grant. Questions
have also arisen about the Shirshov

49
00:04:44,038 --> 00:04:45,880
Institute of Oceanology,

50
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:51,900
which has found itself at the center of major
incidents more than once. One involves a proposal

51
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:58,140
to merge the Institute of Oceanology with
the Kurchatov Institute research center,

52
00:04:58,140 --> 00:05:04,320
which the Russian president supported
several years ago. But the idea met serious

53
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:09,840
resistance from academics, particularly Robert
Nigmatulin, the institute's former director

54
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:16,380
and current scientific director. In 2024,
responding to the wave of criticism,

55
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:24,240
the head of the Kurchatov Institute, Mikhail
Kovalchuk, observed that there were specific

56
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:30,680
interests behind these scandals. Today we will
try to find out who is behind Robert Nigmatulin.”

57
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:40,940
What follows is more of the same
mud these so-called writers

58
00:05:40,940 --> 00:05:45,275
have poured over Robert Iskanderovich.
The material was naturally picked up by

59
00:05:45,275 --> 00:05:46,720
a number of pro-government

60
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:53,320
Telegram channels. And now I'm reading
the following in the outlet Broilernaya:

61
00:05:53,320 --> 00:06:01,520
“Nigmatulin will also have to answer how his
supposedly patriotic position squares with the fact

62
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:05,355
that he lived and worked in the United
States for years, where his children

63
00:06:05,355 --> 00:06:08,320
grew up. His son Tagir worked
in the department of nuclear

64
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:13,219
engineering at Rensselaer Polytechnic
Institute. His daughter Karima

65
00:06:13,219 --> 00:06:15,740
[unclear] the creation of dangerous

66
00:06:15,740 --> 00:06:22,980
viruses, and was even his lover. She is now
married to the son of the aluminum oligarch Vitaly

67
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:29,900
Machitski, who somehow escapes
anti-Russian sanctions. Today

68
00:06:29,900 --> 00:06:34,095
Academician Nigmatulin engages in
populist activity more often than

69
00:06:34,095 --> 00:06:35,660
science, promotes Western

70
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:41,560
values and praises the achievements of Europe
and America. At first his attacks targeted the

71
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:47,840
 government's economic team, but
now he criticizes the president,

72
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:54,880
whom this pseudo-expert blames for all the state's
problems.” Friends, do you recognize this style?

73
00:06:54,880 --> 00:07:05,320
That is why I fear for Robert Iskanderovich's
life and freedom. His work will now be

74
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:09,680
examined under a microscope by the
security services. The institute's

75
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,260
economic activity will be

76
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:16,070
examined. You know the saying: find
the person, and we'll always find an

77
00:07:16,070 --> 00:07:17,940
offense to charge them with.

78
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:24,700
I think using administrative power could
result in Academician Robert Nigmatulin,

79
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:32,370
an outstanding Soviet and Russian
scientist with a clear civic position,

80
00:07:32,370 --> 00:07:34,820
being seriously harmed.

81
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:45,800
His freedom could even be at stake. That
is how I would characterize the situation.

82
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:55,040
Of course I will support Robert Iskanderovich
in every way I can, and I will never believe

83
00:07:55,040 --> 00:08:02,440
that this man could harm the
Russian state or our homeland.

84
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:14,780
The fact that his criticism of the president
makes some of these yapping dogs salivate

85
00:08:14,780 --> 00:08:20,860
is their problem. They're given talking
points and bark at whomever they are told to.

86
00:08:20,860 --> 00:08:28,020
But we cannot allow our country to
reach the point where we are witnessing

87
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:40,400
methods that, unfortunately, existed earlier in
our history and that we ourselves condemned.

88
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:48,981
Now they are returning: accusing,
condemning and harassing a person for

89
00:08:48,981 --> 00:08:51,640
their political views,

90
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:57,815
for criticizing authorities who, in
his opinion, are bringing the country

91
00:08:57,815 --> 00:08:59,760
toward difficult times.

92
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:07,520
Is Robert Iskanderovich Nigmatulin the only one
saying this? I think half the country is saying it.

93
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:17,240
Some speak openly because they have
access to public platforms, as he does.

94
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:27,520
Others speak in private, in smoking rooms or
at the kitchen table. But people are talking.

95
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:35,640
People talk and think about this. And what
is happening today to Robert Iskanderovich—

96
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:40,879
a real harassment campaign in the
so-called best traditions of a

97
00:09:40,879 --> 00:09:43,580
particular period in our history—

98
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:52,780
is no longer just a warning sign. It is an
established fact that once again shows us

99
00:09:52,780 --> 00:10:04,700
what our country is turning into, what is
happening to our state, and what awaits many of us

100
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:12,060
who disagree with the policies of the country's
leadership. Your comments are welcome, as always.
